FAQ = [
 ("What is the best bed rack for a 2019–2023 Ford Ranger?",
  "For a rooftop tent, the ZROADZ Access Overland Rack (Z835201). ZROADZ rates it at 1,500 lb static, 800 lb on-road and 400 lb off-road, the highest figures here, and it clamps on without drilling, with three lifting side gates and an LED kit. The Putco Venture TEC (1,000 lb static, 600 lb dynamic) is the aluminum alternative with a tent kit included. For a brand-name rack that moves to your next truck, Yakima's OutPost HD or OverHaul HD towers."),
 ("Do 2019–2023 Ranger racks fit the 2024+ Ranger?",
  "Don't assume it. The 2024 Ranger has a different bed: about 59.6 in long and 48.2 in between the wheel wells, against 61 in and 44.8 in on the 2019–2023 SuperCrew bed. Some listings cover both, including Putco's 2019–2025 Venture TEC, and ZROADZ lists the Z835201 for 2019–2026. Ask the maker to confirm the part for a newer truck. If you trade up, check the rack against that truck's own list."),
 ("Is there a bed rack for the SuperCab's 6 ft bed?",
  "Fewer one-piece racks cover it. The SuperCab has the 6 ft bed, listed as 6'1\" or 72.7 in, and the Putco listing here is for the 5'1\" bed only. Yakima's clamp towers work by bed rail rather than bed length, so they are the easier route; confirm the fit kit and HD Bar length with Yakima's fit lookup. For any budget rack, ask the seller whether it covers the 6 ft bed before ordering."),
 ("What is the difference between static and dynamic load ratings?",
  "Dynamic, sometimes called on-road, is what the rack should carry while moving, when bumps and braking multiply the load. Static is the parked figure, which matters when people are sleeping in a rooftop tent. ZROADZ rates the Z835201 at 1,500 lb static, 800 lb on-road and 400 lb off-road; Putco rates the Venture TEC at 1,000, 600 and 300 lb. Keep tent and gear under the moving figure, and count the rack against payload."),
 ("How high should a Ranger bed rack be for a rooftop tent?",
  "On Ranger5G, owners in tonneau-and-rack threads suggest bar heights of roughly 8 to 15 in for a tent, with taller racks letting the tent sit above the cab. One owner picked 15 in on an Xtrusion rack available from 10 to 21 in, and his tent slightly overhangs the cab. Yakima's OutPost HD is fixed at 13 in and the OverHaul HD adjusts from 19 to 30 in; the JOYTUTUS stands 14.96 in."),
 ("Can I keep a tonneau cover under a bed rack?",
  "Yes, with a matched pair. Ranger5G owners describe racks bolted to the bed with a roll-up cover passing underneath, noting a rolled cover takes about 5–6 in, so the bars need more clearance than that. Putco says the Venture TEC works with roll-up covers that mount inside the bed rails. Yakima's Tonneau Kit 1 fits select covers. Many budget racks say nothing about covers, so ask before buying."),
 ("Does the ZROADZ rack's weight matter on a Ranger?",
  "It does. ZROADZ lists the Z835201 at 125 lb, before a tent, gear or the cab's passengers, and all of that counts against the payload on your door-jamb sticker. Yakima's OutPost HD towers are 44.09 lb and the OverHaul HD towers 59.52 lb, both before crossbars. If you run a heavy tent and a full crew, a lighter rack leaves more payload for everything else."),
 ("Will a rack stop me using the Ranger's tailgate?",
  "Not usually. The racks here mount to the bed rails or stake pockets and leave the tailgate free. A tent or long load that overhangs the back of the rack can get in the way of dropping the tailgate, so check clearance before you set the tent position. ZROADZ's lifting side gates let you reach the bed from the sides, which helps when the tailgate end is blocked by a load."),
 ("Are cheap overland racks safe for a Ranger tent?",
  "Only within their stated limits, and many don't state much. The JOYTUTUS listing quotes 900 lb with no static and dynamic split, and the OBNAUX pages we read give no rating. Both list the Ranger across several generations. For a sleeping load, choose a rack with published static and dynamic figures, like the ZROADZ or Putco, or get the seller to state them in writing."),
 ("Will a bed rack block the Ranger's third brake light?",
  "The rack itself usually won't, because the third brake light sits at the top of the cab and racks sit behind it. A tent, cargo box or tall load that rises above the roof line can hide it from following drivers. Keep tall loads toward the rear of the rack, and if you add lights to the rack, like the ZROADZ LED kit, check your state's rules on auxiliary lighting."),
]

